    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0203" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg143"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1895</hi></date>. (Received Nov. 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2360.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm my telegram to
                    you of the 20th instant, as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Opposition of China to commission practically finished. Commission will
                            go, unless countermanded.</p></quote></p>
                <p>In this connection I inclose a translation of a communication to me from the
                    Tsung-li Yamên, wherein the suggestion is made that the route of the commission
                    be by water, and that on arriving at the province of Szechuan the members
                    thereof should consult or act with the judge of that province; in other words,
                    he is to be the Chinese commissioner.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d148-a1.xml" xpointer="d148-a1"/>
            </div>
